// Errata for vendor/sysml-v2-release/bnf/KerML-textual-bnf.kebnf (release 2026-08).
//
// The published KEBNF is a hand-maintained rendering of the KerML specification
// grammar. Where it rejects text that the official library and examples use (and the
// Pilot implementation accepts), the corrected rule is given here; tools/sysml/sysml.pl
// reads this file after the published grammar, so a rule here replaces the published
// one. Each erratum: the published rule, the evidence, and why.

// E-K1 Invariant: the feature declaration is optional.
//   Published:  FeaturePrefix 'inv' ( 'true' | isNegated ?= 'false' )? FeatureDeclaration ValuePart? FunctionBody
//   Evidence:   sysml.library/Kernel Libraries/Kernel Data Type Library/Collections.kerml:94
//               inv { flattenedSize == size(elements) }
Invariant =
    FeaturePrefix
    'inv' ( 'true' | isNegated ?= 'false' )?
    FeatureDeclaration? ValuePart?
    FunctionBody

// E-K2 LibraryPackage: 'standard' is optional ('library package' is a user library).
//   Published:  ( isStandard ?= 'standard' ) 'library' ...
//   Evidence:   examples/kerml (library package 'Model Library Example')
LibraryPackage =
    ( isStandard ?= 'standard' )? 'library'
    ( ownedRelationship += PrefixMetadataMember )*
    PackageDeclaration PackageBody
